esto  with lots and lots of policies in it  boris johnson had three words and we  didn't knock it down you said that  you thought that was the right policy do  you still think it was the right policy  yes of course because what we were doing  was we were  we were fighting against a deal that we  thought would be very damaging for our  country  and it is important to remember that for  month after month after month and you  will have seen this  i was standing there putting forward  amendments to get a deal over the line  it was only when we were confronted with  theresa may's deal and then boris  johnson's deal  which i believe will be damaging for the  country that we even entertain the  question of putting it back  uh for people to uh agree or not agree  so  um we i don't know how many times i  pushed amendment for a customs union  and we got within three votes of it had  that succeeded  we would have left with a deal um so we  only moved on to the question of a  second referendum to to protect the  country  uh against a damaging brexit now when  you were talking about issues that  people raised  during the election campaign you also  mentioned anti-semitism yes  now of course you're a member a senior  member of the shadow cabinet what did  you personally do  to try and address the genuine concerns  that many had about anti-semitism in the  labour party i spoke out publicly on the  andrew mar show  on radio 4 on the pester show to say we  must have the international definition  of anti-semitism  to say that those who deny we've got a  problem are part of the problem  to say we need to change our respond to  interview questions what did you do well  i was making that case  the first thing was i was making those  arguments publicly the second thing was  i was making those points in the shadow  cabinet  we had a lot of discussion about  anti-semitism and a lot of challenge  went in in the shadow cabinet  on that now i've not been one to reveal  what's gone in the shadow cabinet  because i believe in collective  responsibility  but you shouldn't read into that that  there weren't very significant  challenges going on in the shadow  cabinet  so for example i was saying in order to  reassure us  we need to have periodic reports of the  shadow cabinet about how we're getting  on with disciplinary cases etc  in the end for me i said that the test  for our party  should now be whether those that have  left our party because of anti-semitism  feel comfortable to return to it and i  said that to louise elman when she  when she left our party and if i was  leader of labour party i would take  personal responsibility for this because  having run a big organization i know  that  if the person if the leader of the  organization has a line of sight  that changes the whole culture within  the organization  okay okay do you think jeremy corbyn had  a blind spot on it  i think jeremy should have been stronger  we should have been quicker on it  um but i don't want to point the finger  at one individual we failed on this  um i would take a different position as  leader of labor party i would make it my  responsibility to rebuild  trust with the jewish community i'd make  it my responsibility i'd say every  friday i need to see a report of how  we're getting on  because if the person at the top of the  organization says  i want to know what's going on every  friday or whatever it is  then in my experience from running a big  organization things change pretty  rapidly  a couple of other points i'm keen to get  in before the end of the interview we're  in glasgow  scotland um could you ever support  a second independence referendum in  scotland well  i don't support uh scotland leaving  the uk i think uh that that would be  damaging for scotland and damaging for  the uk um and so i think we should  be very very strong in making the case  for the united kingdom  i don't think the state i don't think  the status quo is working i do accept  that that's got to change but i don't  think that scotland leaving the uk is  the way forward can you rule out ever  supporting one well i've made  a different case which is for for  federalism a radical federalism and  that's what i believe in so  any manifesto under my leadership would  be putting that forward but i'll say  this just to  finish that answer that whatever  position in the end the labour party  takes it has to be done in agreement  with scottish labour  and i think there's been too much of a  gap between the leader of labour party  and scottish labor  lately and i want to close that gap and  make sure that we're working  together and that's why i've been up  here actually two or three weeks ago  having those discussions  and having further discussions today um  now at the first  leadership hustings yeah last month  we've rewind back seems  like it does it really does it's got a  long long way to go in the contest as  well  um you said i certainly won't be giving  interviews to the sun  during the course of this campaign why  not  well we were in liverpool does that  matter if you're in liverpool  oh it absolutely matters um the history  of hillsborough  and the sun's coverage of it absolutely  speaks for its for itself i think  everybody in liverpool still feels very  very strongly  about that but the sun has also i mean  there's been  within elements of the press elements of  the press i do defend  journalists and it's very important we  do but in elements of the press there's  been  vilification of labour leaders that's  gone on um  for many many years and jeremy corbyn  probably got it worse than any leader  this time and  when we went and knocked on doors and  people said they didn't like jeremy  corbyn  quite a bit of that was what had been  fed into them by  the press and we need we do need to  address this because  in the end if we lose any kind of  balance in the coverage of  politics we're on a slippery slope and  you know you can have an honest  discussion all you like about  politicians and politics  but once you're on that slippery slope  then we're losing touch with  with you know what actually matters i  mean to put the other  argument you know many of those voters  who labor lost at the last election  may well have been sun readers why don't  you want to talk to them well  i am talking to those voters i've spent  a lot of time  across the country talking to voters in  their communities  wherever they are having blunt and  gritty discussions  and that is one of the jobs of the  leader of labour party which is to  listen to people across the country  when you complained when number 10  excluded certain  media outlets from briefings i mean some  would say you're being  hypocritical by refusing there is a  massive difference  between an individual candidate saying  i'm not going to do an interview  with the sun and the prime minister  excluding  a section of the press from even getting  a briefing that there's miles of  difference between the two  okay okay now just finally you're the  last  uh man left in this race and the other  candidates are women now i spoke to  jess phillips who of course dropped out  of the race uh last month and  she said if you truly believe in women's  representation  sometimes passing the mic is the  greatest way to show  that you truly believe in something if  you ever consider passing the mic so  labour can have a female leader well  i've talked to the other candidates  about this because it comes up as you  can imagine  and i've said nobody in this is standing  because they're a man  or because there are women and the other  candidates agree with me we are all  honestly and genuinely putting forward  the case that we think is best for our  party our movement  and our country and uh we're doing that  in a very positive spirit by the way  we're  modeling uh the sort of unity that this  party absolutely needs we're not taking  lumps out of each other  and if we can model it during this  campaign and that's good for the labour  party but in the end our members will  decide having heard our arguments  but what i will say is i know that this  is not the job of one individual  and what i've been saying is don't  support me come alongside me because  this is going to have to be a team  effort  okay thank you very much for being on  the show thank you
 

